<section class="lux-ms-section" id="market-overview"><div class="lux-ms-shell">
  <header class="lux-ms-heading"><div><span class="lux-ms-eyebrow">Market Overview</span><h2>China Market <em>Overview</em></h2></div><p class="lux-ms-lead">In 2025, China's GDP reached <strong>RMB 140.188 trillion</strong>, with real growth of <strong>5.0%</strong>.</p></header>
  <div class="lux-ms-stats" aria-label="Key China market data for 2025"><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-card-explanation="China's economic scale supports many premium-import consumption settings and gives LuxurEat a broad foundation for long-term local cooperation."><strong>RMB 140.188 trillion</strong><span>2025 GDP</span></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-card-explanation="Steady real growth points to expanding demand and commercial activity, offering a resilient environment for Italy–China trade projects."><strong>+5.0%</strong><span>Real GDP growth</span></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-card-explanation="Manufacturing growth signals strengthening supply-chain and production capacity, supporting LuxurEat's sourcing and manufacturing partnerships."><strong>+6.1%</strong><span>Manufacturing growth</span></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-card-explanation="Continued services growth supports a more mature commercial base for import distribution, brand entry and project coordination."><strong>+5.4%</strong><span>Services growth</span></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-card-explanation="Rapid digital-services growth helps LuxurEat connect with China through local websites, ecommerce and digital channels more efficiently."><strong>+11.1%</strong><span>Information, software and IT services growth</span></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-card-explanation="Growth in accommodation and catering creates more occasions for Italian wine and premium foods across hospitality, dining and experience-led consumption."><strong>+4.9%</strong><span>Accommodation and catering growth</span></article></div>
  <div class="lux-ms-prose lux-ms-prose-after"><p>China is not a single market. There are clear differences between coastal and inland areas, mature metropolises and emerging cities, and traditional channels and digital ecosystems. National data is therefore more useful as market context, while specific projects still need to be assessed by city, channel and product category.</p></div>
  <p class="lux-ms-source"><strong>Data source: National Bureau of Statistics of China, 2025.</strong></p>
</div></section>
<section class="lux-ms-section is-light" id="cities"><div class="lux-ms-shell">
  <header class="lux-ms-heading"><div><span class="lux-ms-eyebrow">Cities &amp; Economic Centres</span><h2>Cities &amp; <em>Economic Centres</em></h2></div><p class="lux-ms-lead">Business opportunities in China are distributed across multiple cities and regions. In addition to major economic centres such as Beijing, Shanghai, Guangzhou, Chengdu and Chongqing, a number of cities are also maintaining relatively rapid growth.</p></header>
  <span class="lux-ms-eyebrow">Major International Business Centres</span>
  <div class="lux-ms-card-grid"><article class="lux-ms-card" tabindex="0"><h3>Shanghai</h3><p>One of China's most important international trade and business centres, and a key point of entry for imported goods, international brands and professional services.</p></article><article class="lux-ms-card" tabindex="0"><h3>Beijing</h3><p>An important national political, economic and business centre, with a high concentration of corporate headquarters and institutional resources.</p></article><article class="lux-ms-card" tabindex="0"><h3>Guangzhou</h3><p>An important trade and business centre in South China, closely connected to food, catering, wholesale, import and exhibition markets.</p></article><article class="lux-ms-card" tabindex="0"><h3>Shenzhen</h3><p>An important centre for technology, innovation and the digital economy, and a major business node in the Guangdong–Hong Kong–Macao Greater Bay Area.</p></article><article class="lux-ms-card" tabindex="0"><h3>Chengdu &amp; Chongqing</h3><p>Important consumer and business centres in western China, offering a market environment different from coastal cities for companies seeking inland expansion.</p></article></div>
  <div class="lux-market-growth" data-market-copy-group><span class="lux-ms-eyebrow">High-growth cities · Real GDP growth in selected cities in 2025</span><div class="lux-ms-stats"><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-explanation="Hefei leads the selected cities, signalling stronger commercial momentum in inland growth markets and new consumption and channel opportunities for LuxurEat."><strong>Hefei<br>+6.1%</strong></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-explanation="Wuhan's steady growth reinforces its appeal as a Central China hub and a useful gateway for inland distribution of imported foods."><strong>Wuhan<br>+5.6%</strong></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-explanation="Shenzhen combines economic growth with digital and innovation strengths, creating favourable conditions for LuxurEat's brand and premium-consumer partnerships."><strong>Shenzhen<br>+5.5%</strong></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-explanation="Suzhou's growth and Yangtze River Delta industrial base can connect premium products with mature supply chains and consumer markets."><strong>Suzhou<br>+5.4%</strong></article><article class="lux-ms-stat" tabindex="0" data-market-explanation="Hangzhou's growth and active digital ecosystem offer favourable conditions for LuxurEat to explore ecommerce and brand-content channels."><strong>Hangzhou<br>+5.2%</strong></article></div><div class="lux-ms-prose lux-ms-prose-after"><p data-market-copy-target>A city's growth rate alone does not represent the market potential of a particular product, but it can help companies identify the pace of development and changing commercial focus across different regions of China.</p></div></div>
  <p class="lux-ms-source"><strong>Data sources: National Bureau of Statistics of China and related official statistics, 2025.</strong></p>
</div></section>
